  "description": "<p>Steps to reproduce:</p>\n\n<p>1. Navigate to a binary in the web console<br/>\n2. Select a file and click \"update\"<br/>\n3. The operation fails with a 400</p>\n\n<p>The root cause is that the HTTP request is passing an empty Content-Type header. Relevant code: <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-webapp/src/main/webapp/static/js/common.js#L242\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-webapp/src/main/webapp/static/js/common.js#L242</a></p>\n\n<p>This should likely be addressed by giving the user a way to specify the desired mime type. Ideally, prepopulated with the current type.</p>",
